      "verified": true,
      "evidence": "Last week without EMEA: 7310 / 309400 / 26710. 7600/7310=+3.97%, 319100/309400=+3.14%, 27200/26710=+1.83%."
    },
    {
      "claim": "EMEA was ~33% of each metric last week",
      "type": "factual",
      "verified": true,
      "evidence": "3580/10890=32.9%, 152900/462300=33.1%, 12870/39580=32.5%."
    },
    {
      "claim": "Average order value slipped in every region (NA £44.3 → £43.9)",
      "type": "factual",
      "verified": true,
      "evidence": "NA 44.28→43.92, APAC 41.26→40.90, LATAM 36.15→35.90."
    },
    {
      "claim": "The headline drop is a data-coverage gap, not a business decline",
      "type": "quality",
      "verified": false,
      "evidence": "Plausible, but the files can't establish it. The reviewer itself admits it could be 'a real outage'. Stating it as fact in a leadership document goes beyond the evidence."
